    kgjobs:sourceRecordId "remote-senior-content-and-social-media-manager-342403" ;
    schema:datePosted "2026-08-22"^^xsd:date ;
    schema:description "🚀 About Nivoda Nivoda is a fast-growing B2B marketplace that is transforming the global diamond and gemstone industry. We connect buyers and sellers across the world, processing $300M+ in annual transactions and unlocking a $350B industry opportunity. We move fast, think big, and care deeply about the businesses and people we serve. 🌍 Our Mission The diamond trading industry has historically been fragmented, opaque, and inaccessible. Nivoda was founded to change that: to empower businesses of all sizes and locations to participate in a fair, efficient global marketplace. Every line of code, every integration, every automation we build brings us closer to that mission. 🤔 About the Role We are looking for a Sr. Content and Social Media Manager to own our social channels and be the creative engine behind our marketing campaigns. You are a storyteller first and an operator second: you can take an idea, shape it into something people actually want to watch and share, and make it show up consistently everywhere we publish. This is a connective role. You will own the content calendar, plan and run campaigns end to end, keep a strong and consistent presence on social, and run our newsletter. You will be the glue across marketing, making sure a campaign lands as one coherent story across social, email, and beyond rather than a set of disconnected posts. As the team grows we will add editorial depth alongside you (long-form writing and podcast production), so you can stay focused on what you do best: social, storytelling, and campaigns that move. What would you be doing? Own Nivoda’s social media channels end to end, from strategy and calendar to publishing and community, with Instagram and our primary channels front and centre. Be the main creative force behind our marketing campaigns: come up with the idea, shape the story, and make it show up consistently across every channel. Own the content calendar and keep every channel in sync, so campaigns land as one coherent story rather than scattered posts. Plan and run campaigns end to end: the brief, the timeline, the assets, the launch, and the follow-through. Run \"The Modern Jewellers Playbook\", our newsletter. Own the cadence and the sends, and tie it into everything else we are publishing. Turn our bigger content moments, like interviews, launches, and guides, into a steady stream of social-first content that travels. Write social and short-form copy that sounds like a real person and makes independent jewellers stop scrolling. Work with our designer and video partners to ship content that looks as good as it reads, and with our paid marketer to amplify what is working. Be the connective tissue across marketing: link events, campaigns, and content so nothing happens in a silo. Track what performs across channels and use it to sharpen the calendar. Double down on what lands, and drop what does not. What do we need from you? 4+ years running social and content for a brand, with real ownership of channels and campaigns rather than just scheduling posts. You are a storyteller first. You know how to take an idea and make it land as a post, an email, a thread, or a reel. A body of social and campaign work you are proud of, ideally including channels you grew yourself. You can write. Quickly, well, and in a voice that sounds human rather than corporate. Sharp project management. You can run a content calendar and several campaigns at once without dropping any threads. Comfort working hands-on on a small team and building process where none exists. Fluent with the tools of modern social and content work, and happy to lean on AI to move faster. An instinct for what performs, and the discipline to let data settle the debates. Nice to have Knowledge of the jewelry industry Experience marketing to small business owners, retailers, or a trade and craft audience. Hands-on with short-form video: you can shoot and cut a reel yourself, or confidently direct someone who can. Experience running an email or newsletter program. Community-building experience, online or off. Our culture and what we offer We're a high-growth company in an exponential expansion phase. We move fast, operate with low hierarchy, and give people real ownership from day one. If you want to work somewhere you can genuinely shape things: not just maintain them: Nivoda is the place. Our current benefits 🕐 Flexible working hours and vibrant company culture 🏡 Remote work 📈 Opportunities for growth and learning 🌴 Unlimited holiday allowance 🚀 Chance to join during our exponential expansion phase Equal Opportunity Nivoda is an equal opportunity employer. We celebrate diversity and are committed to creating an inclusive environment for all employees. Even if it seems you don't meet 100% of our musts, don't let that stop you from applying: we hire for potential and mindset, not just a checklist. Please submit your CV in English. Not quite the right role? If this role isn't for you but you're excited about Nivoda, join our Talent Pool and we'll reach out when something's a better fit: nivoda.com/talent-pool Find Jobs in Germany on Arbeitnow" ;
